## The docs to read

Standing: {{.inputs.standing}}

Catalog: {{.inputs.catalog}}

Templates: {{.inputs.templates}}

Open them with `read_file`. Read the template for this concept's kind and follow its headings. You can read the docs of this layer and the layers above it, and nothing else.

## What to produce

`doc`: the complete doc, frontmatter included, on the template.

`doc_path`: `docs/<id>.md`.

`questions`: what only a person can settle and the docs cannot. Each `{ name, header, question, description, options: [{ value, description }], default, custom: true, optional: true }`. The default is the reading you took, as one of the options.

`standing_amendment`: only when a standing doc is wrong.

`responses`: nothing on a first pass.

## The critique could not close these

{{.inputs.findings}}

Turn every finding you cannot settle from the docs into a `questions` entry, in the shape the brief gave. Settle from the docs what the docs settle. Re-emit `doc` and `doc_path` in full, and `responses` with each finding `blocked` and its question named.

## What the person said

{{.inputs.comments}}

Apply it. Re-emit `doc`, `doc_path` and `questions` in full.
